\section{Conclusion}
\label{sec:future-work}
OU--III combines a 21-state quaternion MEKF, an exactly discretized OU chain,
and measurement-driven SpectralMSE integral regularization. The ten-seed
stationary JONSWAP comparison reduces normalized vertical RMS from
$\OUValidationOUIINormalizedMean\%$ to $\OUValidationOUIIINormalizedMean\%$
of incident $H_s$. The four-arm ablation attributes most of the off-nominal
benefit to adaptive $r_S$, rather than OU scheduling alone. PM--Stokes and
3-D results support the axis-dependent OU--III configuration within the
prescribed vessel-response ensemble; TFG differences remain channel dependent.

Low-motion noise floors, bias ambiguity, and severe unmitigated vibration
limit performance. Vibration filtering and covariance inflation reduce,
but do not eliminate, reconstruction error. The output is oscillatory
motion about a local reference, not absolute navigation position.
Externally referenced trials across hulls and headings, thermal and magnetic
calibration, and evaluation of the full-state physical MSE remain priorities.
Embedded execution establishes portability, not measured resource or deadline margins.
